3.1. Energy consuming subsystems and their power models
A typical SLM machine consists of various energy consuming subsystems. Among them, the computer, screen, control unit, light work together to ensure the operational readiness of the machine. They also work during the whole manufacturing process, and thus, are deﬁned as basic subsystem. The heater can heat the platform to avoid distortion caused by uneven distribution of temperature of the manufactured parts and the high temperature difference between the scanned powders and adjacent powders. The cooling system is further divided into water circulation unit and water-cooling unit, which are used to cool down the optical elements and the laser. The lasers expose the build ﬁeld via a 3D scan optic to melt the metal powder. The re-coater motor moves to distribute a layer of metal powder on the substrate plate. The gas circulation system includes the electric valves which control the gas inlet and outlet and gas circulation pump motor which drives the pump to convey the inert gas in the circuit to free the process atmosphere of metal particles. The powder vibrating sieving machine sieves and separates metal powder with proper grain sizes.

