The powers of heater, water circulation unit, water-cooling unit, recoater motor, electric valves, gas circulation pump motor and powder vibrating sieve are constant, which can be obtained from the rated power on the nameplate of the motors or measurements. In comparison, the power of laser varies with the output power. The SLM machines are often equipped with ﬁbre lasers. During the working process, the input energy is used to excite light which is propagating in the optical ﬁbre. There are inevitable losses due to the quantum defect, excess pump, signal losses and non-optimised cavity (Zervas and Codemard 2014). Suppose the energy conversion efﬁciencies is η, the power consumption of laser can be estimated as a linear function of laser output power.

PL = n(PL1 + PLo/η)

