The case study has demonstrated the effectiveness of the proposed methodology. The model input parameters, including the product volume and height, area of outer and inner surfaces of the fabricated parts, machine settings and process parameters, could be obtained from process preparing software, such as SLM MCS 2.2 (see Figure 4(a)). This implies that the proposed model could be easily integrated with the existing software and applied as a tool for estimating the energy demand of the SLM process to enhance its sustainability. Based on the proposed method, measures including shortening process time, increasing the number of parts in a single build and switching off the machine subsystems when not in use, could be developed to reduce the energy consumption of SLM process.

6. Conclusions and future work
As one of the most promising AM technologies, SLM has experienced notable increases in manufacturing industrial in recent years, which results in increased electricity consumption. It is imperative to forecast this part of energy for environmental impact analysis and energy reduction purpose. The contributions and ﬁndings of this paper can be summarised as follows:
• This paper proposed a novel method that uses the power models of machine subsystems, time models of sub processes and machine subsystem working status to forecast the energy consumption of SLM processes.
• The power data of each machine subsystem is obtained by measurement and the laser power model is acquired through statistical analysis of the measured data. The time of each sub-process is modelled as a function of product volume and height, area of outer and inner surfaces of the fabricated parts, process parameters and machine operating parameters.
• The effectiveness of the proposed method is demonstrated by two case studies. The prediction accuracy of the proposed method is signiﬁcantly better than those of the speciﬁc energy model, stage- and subsystem-based energy models.
• The subsystem level and sub-process level energy consumption breakdown can be obtained using the proposed method, which makes the energy ﬂow more transparent.

