The proposed energy model can be easily integrated within lifecycle analysis, product design, process design and task scheduling applications given its very simple formulation. The method presented here could be used for other AM processes such as SLA, SLS and EBM with modiﬁcations of process type and time and power study. One limitation of the study is that the product geometry, laser jump time and scan control of multi-laser system are not involved. Future work will be conducted to investigate the inﬂuence of product geometry, laser jump time and multi-laser scan strategy on process energy consumption and assess how the proposed method can be extended and generalised for other AM processes. Detailed time and power study, as well as energy consumption measurements will be conducted to assess the feasibility of the proposed method on other AM processes.

